The group is `8` permutations of `Fin 8`, the excess permutations that pin it from above are `9`,
and the invariant family it acts on has `16,777,216` members. How many of those have this group as
their automorphism group *exactly* is not computed and does not need to be: the family is indexed by
the subtype `Magma.tup8R9` of transport tuples passing `Magma.tupOK`, and both sides of the
rectangle are decided by search rather than by enumeration. See `Definability/ExactPrune.lean` for
the device and `Definability/Srch_S8R9.lean` for the data lemmas.

This file is generated by `genrect.py`; it holds only tables, so that `native_decide` -- which
recompiles its whole enclosing module on each invocation -- never has to compile them twice.
-/

